#: ckanext/theme_ldm_tib/templates/home/ldm_register.html:14
msgid "LDM visitors"
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/theme_ldm_tib/templates/home/ldm_register.html:15
msgid ""
"Any visitor of the website is able to navigate the site, perform searches over the public datasets, preview and/or download the available public resources "
"without restrictions."
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/theme_ldm_tib/templates/home/ldm_register.html:16
msgid "Users, organizations and authorization"
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/theme_ldm_tib/templates/home/ldm_register.html:17
msgid ""
"LDM users can register user accounts and log in. Login is not needed to search for and find data, but is needed for all publishing functions: datasets can be"
" created, edited, etc by users with the appropriate permissions. In LDM all research data is managed within Organizations and Groups. An Organization is an "
"institution or entity where the researcher/s is/are affiliated."
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/theme_ldm_tib/templates/home/ldm_register.html:18
msgid "Registering to the platform"
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/theme_ldm_tib/templates/home/ldm_register.html:22
#, python-format
msgid ""
"In case an organization or group wants to be added to LDM, the responsible or representative must contact LDM's sysadmin asking for the creation of the "
"organization or group in the system and creation of an administrator user to it. For this please email %(contact_link)s."
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/theme_ldm_tib/templates/home/ldm_register.html:23
msgid ""
"After receiving the solitude, LDM's System Administrators will create the Organization and Groups and assign an \"Administrator\" user to them. A new "
"registered user is not able to create datasets until a role is assigned."
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/theme_ldm_tib/templates/home/ldm_register.html:24
msgid ""
"<b>Organizations</b> are controlling which users can add, update and publish which datasets. Every dataset in LDM must belong to exactly one organization. If"
" a user is an editor or admin of an organization, then he or she can create new datasets in that organization, and can edit and publish the datasets that "
"belong to that organization."
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/theme_ldm_tib/templates/home/ldm_register.html:25
msgid ""
"<b>Groups</b> are about curation – collecting datasets together into groups, across organisational boundaries. If a user is an editor or admin of a group, "
"then he or she can add datasets (that already exist on the website) into their group and can remove datasets from their group, but they cannot add new "
"datasets to the site, or edit the datasets that are in their group. Groups are intended for collecting related datasets together into themes like \"climate\""
" etc."
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/theme_ldm_tib/templates/home/ldm_register.html:26
msgid "LDM allows administrator users to add members (users) to organizations/groups with three kind of roles:"
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/theme_ldm_tib/templates/home/ldm_register.html:27
msgid "For organizations"
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/theme_ldm_tib/templates/home/ldm_register.html:29
msgid "Member – can see the organization's private datasets"
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/theme_ldm_tib/templates/home/ldm_register.html:30
msgid "Editor – can edit and publish datasets"
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/theme_ldm_tib/templates/home/ldm_register.html:31
msgid "Admin – can add, remove and change roles for organization members"
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/theme_ldm_tib/templates/home/ldm_register.html:33
msgid "For groups"
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/theme_ldm_tib/templates/home/ldm_register.html:35
msgid "Member – can add/remove datasets from groups"
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/theme_ldm_tib/templates/home/ldm_register.html:36
msgid "Admin – can edit group information, as well as manage group's members."
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/theme_ldm_tib/templates/home/ldm_register.html:38
msgid "To be able to add members to organizations/groups the new user must ask the administrator user her/his addition bringing her/his email and personal data."
msgstr ""

